+      "answer": "Standard anatomical position is the reference pose: standing upright, facing forward, feet flat and slightly apart, arms at sides with palms facing forward, and thumbs pointing outward. All directional terms assume this position."
+    },
+    {
+      "question": "Q2. What are the three major body planes?",
+      "answer": "Sagittal (divides left/right), coronal/frontal (divides front/back), and transverse/horizontal (divides top/bottom)."
+    },
+    {
+      "question": "Q3. What is the difference between anterior and posterior?",
+      "answer": "Anterior (ventral) means toward the front of the body; posterior (dorsal) means toward the back."
+    },
+    {
+      "question": "Q4. What does proximal versus distal mean?",
+      "answer": "Proximal means closer to the point of attachment to the trunk; distal means farther away (used mainly for limbs)."
