+        "headers": [
+          "Layer",
+          "Name",
+          "Key Structures",
+          "Function"
+        ],
+        "rows": [
+          [
+            "Outer (fibrous)",
+            "Tunica fibrosa",
+            "Cornea, sclera",
+            "Protection and shape; cornea refracts light"
+          ],
+          [
+            "Middle (vascular)",
+            "Tunica vasculosa (uvea)",
+            "Iris, ciliary body, choroid",
+            "Blood supply; iris controls pupil size"
+          ],
+          [
+            "Inner (nervous)",
+            "Tunica interna (retina)",
+            "Photoreceptors, bipolar cells, ganglion cells",
+            "Converts light to neural signals"
+          ]
+        ]
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "2-key-internal-structures",
+      "heading": "2. Key Internal Structures",
+      "paragraphs": [
+        "Light path through the eye: Cornea → Aqueous humor → Pupil → Lens → Vitreous humor → Retina → Optic nerve → Brain"
+      ],
+      "bullets": [
+        "Cornea: Transparent front surface; does ~2/3 of light refraction.",
+        "Iris: Colored part; adjusts pupil diameter to control light entry.",
+        "Pupil: Central opening; lets light into the eye.",
+        "Lens: Fine-focuses light onto the retina; changes shape via ciliary muscles (accommodation).",
+        "Vitreous humor: Gel-like substance filling the main cavity; maintains shape.",
+        "Retina: Contains rods (dim light) and cones (color, detail).",
+        "Macula & fovea: Central retina for sharp, detailed vision.",
