+    "The liver lies mainly beneath the right dome of the diaphragm, with part extending across the midline. Its diaphragmatic surface follows the diaphragm; its visceral surface faces a",
+    "The porta hepatis is a gateway on the visceral surface. The hepatic portal vein brings nutrient-rich blood from much of the gastrointestinal tract and spleen; the hepatic artery br",
